From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 10:29:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: send the visible frame size to gen1 encoder
 firmware

The gen1 encoder sent the firmware the padded source (fmt_src: width
aligned to 128, height to 32) as the input frame size, and the CAPTURE
format as the output size. When the two differ the firmware sets up a
scale. At 1280x720 the input is 1280x736 and the output 1280x720, and on
AR50_LITE (QCM2290/SM6115), which has no scaler, the firmware rejects the
session with HFI_ERR_SESSION_UNSUPPORTED_PROPERTY for
HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_VPE_ROTATION (0x3007001):

  qcom-iris 5a00000.video-codec: session error for command: 3007001,
  event id:1007

On a MANGMI Air X (SM6115, venus-6.0 gen1 firmware), H.264 and HEVC at
1280x720 and at 854x480 (padded to 896x480) failed this way. 1920x1080
and 1280x768 encoded, 1920x1080 as a 1920x1088 picture with the padding
rows in it.

Send the visible size, enc_raw_*, as the input and the requested size,
enc_scale_*, as the output, as Qualcomm's msm_vidc driver does on both
SM8250 and SM6115 (msm_venc_set_frame_size() sends the client's unpadded
sizes) and as the gen2 path does with HFI_PROP_RAW_RESOLUTION. The padding
still reaches the firmware through
HFI_PROPERTY_PARAM_UNCOMPRESSED_PLANE_ACTUAL_INFO (stride and scanlines),
and the firmware crops the coded size in the SPS.

With this, all four sizes encode on the Air X for both codecs: 1920x1080
is now 1920x1080 coded as 1088 (PSNR 51.0 dB H.264, 41.3 dB HEVC against
the source), 1280x720 HEVC is coded as 736, 854x480 as 864x480, and the
pictures are intact. SM8250 takes the same path and is untested.

Signed-off-by: sunshineinabox <aqemail@gmail.com>
---
 .../qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c         | 23 +++++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
index f6e9cbfccd09..15e0fca282d6 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1_command.c
@@ -794,20 +794,29 @@ static int iris_hfi_gen1_set_resolution(struct iris_inst *inst, u32 plane)
 
 	if (!iris_drc_pending(inst) && !(inst->sub_state & IRIS_INST_SUB_FIRST_IPSC)) {
 		fs.buffer_type = HFI_BUFFER_INPUT;
-		fs.width = inst->fmt_src->fmt.pix_mp.width;
-		fs.height = inst->fmt_src->fmt.pix_mp.height;
+		if (inst->domain == ENCODER) {
+			/* The visible size: the padding is in the plane info */
+			fs.width = inst->enc_raw_width;
+			fs.height = inst->enc_raw_height;
+		} else {
+			fs.width = inst->fmt_src->fmt.pix_mp.width;
+			fs.height = inst->fmt_src->fmt.pix_mp.height;
+		}
 
 		ret = hfi_gen1_set_property(inst, ptype, &fs, sizeof(fs));
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
 	}
-	if (inst->domain == DECODER)
+	if (inst->domain == DECODER) {
 		fs.buffer_type = HFI_BUFFER_OUTPUT2;
-	else
+		fs.width = inst->fmt_dst->fmt.pix_mp.width;
+		fs.height = inst->fmt_dst->fmt.pix_mp.height;
+	} else {
+		/* Not the coded size, or the firmware takes it for a scale */
 		fs.buffer_type = HFI_BUFFER_OUTPUT;
-
-	fs.width = inst->fmt_dst->fmt.pix_mp.width;
-	fs.height = inst->fmt_dst->fmt.pix_mp.height;
+		fs.width = inst->enc_scale_width;
+		fs.height = inst->enc_scale_height;
+	}
 
 	return hfi_gen1_set_property(inst, ptype, &fs, sizeof(fs));
 }
